# Data Access & Mutation Patterns

## Data Retrieval — Server Components only

All data fetching must happen inside **React Server Components**. Never fetch data in Client Components, route handlers, or via `useEffect`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — fetch inside a Server Component
// app/decks/page.tsx
import { db } from '@/db';
import { decks } from '@/db/schema';
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { eq } from 'drizzle-orm';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

export default async function DecksPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) redirect('/'); // no dedicated sign-in page — homepage has sign-in/sign-up buttons

  const userDecks = await db.select().from(decks).where(eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId));
  return <DeckList decks={userDecks} />;
}

// ❌ BAD — fetching in a Client Component
'use client';
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/decks').then(...);
}, []);
```

## Mutations — Server Actions only

All `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, and `DELETE` operations must be performed inside **Server Actions**. Never mutate the database from a Client Component directly or via API route handlers.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — mutation in a Server Action
'use server';
import { db } from '@/db';
import { decks } from '@/db/schema';
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error('Unauthenticated');
  // ...validate, then insert
  await db.insert(decks).values({ clerkUserId: userId, ...input });
}

// ❌ BAD — mutation inside an API route or client fetch
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json();
  await db.insert(decks).values(body);
}
```

## Validation — Zod required for all Server Actions

Every Server Action **must** validate its inputs with a **Zod schema** before touching the database. Never trust raw client input.

## Typed inputs — no `FormData`

Server Action parameters must be typed with a **TypeScript type or interface** derived from a Zod schema. Never use `FormData` as the parameter type.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { z } from 'zod';

const CreateDeckSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  description: z.string().max(500).optional(),
});

type CreateDeckInput = z.infer<typeof CreateDeckSchema>;

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const parsed = CreateDeckSchema.safeParse(input);
  if (!parsed.success) throw new Error('Invalid input');
  // proceed with parsed.data
}

// ❌ BAD — untyped / unvalidated
export async function createDeck(formData: FormData) {
  const name = formData.get('name');
  await db.insert(decks).values({ name });
}
```

## Rules summary

- **Read** data only in Server Components.
- **Write** data only in Server Actions (`'use server'`).
- **Validate** every Server Action input with Zod before any DB call.
- **Type** every Server Action parameter with a TypeScript type (`z.infer<typeof Schema>`), never `FormData`.
